(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2800010500-magatama-host-sdk-kysely-to-kotobase")
  (:adr/title "The magatama host SDK's data layer moves off kysely/Postgres onto kotobase")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-02")
  (:adr/body "## Decision

**The magatama host SDK's data layer moves off kysely/Postgres onto kotobase
and the kotoba-lang org's own SDKs.** Owner instruction, 2026-09-02:
「kysely などは使わず kotoba-lang org, kotobase, kotoba lang org repo の sdk を
使ってね」.

This ADR records the direction and the measured surface. It does NOT claim the
migration is done — nothing of it is.

## Where kysely actually is

Not in the appviews. `cloud-itonami/media` declared `kysely` and `pg` with
**zero imports anywhere in the repo** and was already querying kotobase
(`dmQuery` / `dmTransact` send Datalog EDN to kotobase.net over XRPC, queries
built by its ClojureScript core). Those declarations were removed
(cloud-itonami/media 4cce02c6) — tidying, not a fix.

The real holder is **`gftdcojp/magatama-host-sdk`**, the shared host layer for
four appviews: cloud-itonami/media, cloud-itonami/news, gftdcojp/ai-gftd-media,
gftdcojp/mamori.

Fourteen modules reach the database through it:

    actor-registry  agent-lifecycle  app  consent-helpers  heartbeat-cadence
    hyperdrive-dialect  index  kami-avatar-pipeline  kysely  mcp-bpmn-router
    mcp-registry-loader  metering  private-write  write-outbox

## What makes this tractable

- **One seam.** Every module goes through `createKyselyDb` in `src/kysely.ts`
  (57 lines). There is no second path to Postgres.
- **A beachhead exists.** `src/kotobase-auth.ts` and `src/kotobase-d1.ts` are
  already here, and the test suite already carries `kotobase-auth.test.ts`.
- **Workers already cannot reach the database.** ADR-2605111200 made
  `createKyselyDb` throw `WorkerDBProhibitedError` inside CF Workers; only the
  Bun/Node pod path connects, through Hyperdrive. So the live consumer surface
  is narrower than fourteen modules suggests.

## What is NOT a drop-in, and must be decided

`net-kotobase/sdk` (`@net-kotobase/sdk`, TypeScript) is the published query
client, but it cannot replace this layer as it stands:

1. **It is read-only.** Six query families, no transact. The host SDK writes
   heavily — outbox, actor registry, metering, agent lifecycle.
2. **It addresses data by `database` / `collections`, with no graph-CID
   parameter.** That is exactly how the appviews address their data
   (`graph: await graphCid(label)`).
3. **Different wire.** The SDK posts
   `/xrpc/ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.query.execute`; the appviews post
   `/xrpc/ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.datomic.q` and `.transact`.

**Whether `query.execute` is deployed is UNVERIFIED from here.** kotobase.net
returns 401 for it — but it returns 401 for `com.example.nope` as well, so the
auth gate sits in front of routing and that probe distinguishes nothing. Do not
read those 401s as evidence the endpoint exists.

## Interim state, and why it is not the destination

magatama-host-sdk 1d634bc4 takes kysely `^0.27.4` -> `^0.28.17`, closing three
HIGH advisories (GHSA-8cpq-38p9-67gx MySQL injection via `sql.lit()`;
GHSA-pv5w-4p9q-p3v2 JSON-path traversal injection; GHSA-wmrf-hv6w-mr66 SQL
injection via unsanitized JSON path keys).

That is a bridge. Leaving three HIGH injection advisories live in a shared SDK
while the migration is planned is not a way to honour the direction.

Measured before landing, because 0.27 -> 0.28 is a breaking window for a typed
query builder and **this repo has no typechecker of its own**: vitest gives the
same 7 failures / 305 passes before and after, same test names; tsc (installed
only to ask the question) gives the same 3 errors at both versions, same files
and lines, differing only in kysely's own message text.

An earlier pass of that A/B reported the opposite — 0.28 breaking, 0.27 clean.
It was wrong: `npm install --no-save kysely@X` had pruned typescript, so tsc
was absent and `grep -c 'error TS'` counted zero against a shell error. **A
check that could not run returned the same value as a check that ran and found
nothing** (ADR-2608136000, question 2). The harness now reinstalls the
toolchain with each version and refuses rather than answers without tsc.

## Also found

`kotoba-lang/app-scap` uses `@supabase/supabase-js` for real — a realtime
adapter under `resources/adapters/supabase/`, not a vestigial declaration.
Same direction applies; separate work, separate decision. It is also a
Next.js/React app, which ADR-2608260900 already places on the cljs +
reagent + re-frame + jp-go-dds path.

No other external database SDK is present workspace-wide: drizzle, prisma,
knex, better-sqlite3, mysql2, typeorm, sequelize, mongodb, redis and
@planetscale/database are all at zero.

## Next step

Decide the write path before touching the fourteen modules. Either
`@net-kotobase/sdk` gains transact plus graph-CID addressing, or the host SDK
keeps its own XRPC client against `datomic.transact` and adopts the SDK only
for reads. That choice is upstream of every module change, and it needs the
question this ADR could not answer: which kotobase XRPC methods are actually
deployed.")))
